# z = x + y, entry by entry, on arrays the program supplies: the step guards every limb
# before it is added (rule R3; milestone2.md, "Arrays that the program fills").
# A map (milestone2.md, "Folds", "sum, dot, axpy, convolution"): every element of z is the step
# on one element of each array read, in any order; the mask finite is the and of the
# tests of the written elements, and when it is false a second pass makes every element that
# is not finite the canonical NaN ("When something is not finite").
fold:          add_2_entry
arrays:        supplied x = x0 x1, supplied y = y0 y1
state:         mask finite
step:          z = add_entry_step_2(x, y)
combine:       finite = and(finite, finite)
orders:        sequential, lanes
writes:        z = z0 z1
check:         fold_finish_2
finish:        none
value:         x+y
requires:      canonical x
requires:      canonical y
ensures:       entries z
ensures:       finite_or_nan z flag=finite
min_precision: 3
theorem:       proofs/theories/FoldMaps.v
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeFoldMaps.v
status:        proved
domain:        extended
source:        add_2_2 (JMP17 Alg. 6, bound from MR22) on each element, guarded
license:       algorithm: published; proof: MIT
